  "term": "twitching",
  "definition": "Twitching is a form of bacterial movement discussed here as one of the motility behaviors of Pseudomonas aeruginosa. In this source, it is linked to type IV pili function and was reduced when the bacteria were exposed to increasing concentrations of 5-fluorouracil.",
